           The European Competence Center on Inclusive Child Participation is a shared space for learning, exchange, and collaboration. It brings together organizations, institutions, practitioners, and most importantly-children and young people to strengthen how children participate in decisions that affect their lives.
            The Competence Center is part of the European Child Participation Network (ECPN) and is supported by the Inclusive Child Participation Networks (ICPN)-a European initiative coordinated by Save the Children Europe and SOS Children’s Villages International, together with partners in 11 countries.
